Hello everyone, 

Greetings tacticians! Since launch, we’ve been collecting your feedback and working on improvements to evolve Sword Legacy: Omen into the best experience possible. We’re now presenting our first update to address some issues you may have encountered:. 

[b]Change Log Build V1.1.1[/b]
[list][*]Items which can be shared by every party member are indicated in their description;
[*]Inside the inventory or shops, item backgrounds turn red if an item can’t be equipped by the currently selected character;
[*]Recommended heroes now have a star icon added to their portrait;
[*]The Talent section of the inventory has a different  background;
[*]There’s now an option to disable the grunts when selecting a character and adjust its volume;
[*]The filling inside regions highlighted had been fixed, and an inner glow has been added to make it more comfortable to the eye;
[*]The position of a Recommended hero’s dialog during party selection has been adjusted;
[*]There are now tooltips informing players about the Gravely Wounded status, what it does and how to cure it;
[*]There’s a tutorial for inspecting enemies in the second combat at “Failed Vows”;
[*]The animation speed of interactive objects has been adjusted. Players can now move right after breaking something;
[*]In the “House of Penance” quest, when the player pulls the lever that activates the traps, the camera moves to show what happened;
[*]Problems with the grid when using “Sacred Ground”, “Mind Trick”, “Holy Word”, “Weakness”, “Phantasm”, “Bless Armor” and “Bless Weapon” close to walls or blocked areas have been solved;
[*]The “missing click” error with the “Firewall” skill has been resolved;
[*]Inconsistencies with the “Taunt” skill depending on the location have been solved;
[*]The issue with character speeches which didn’t change properly in cutscenes has been addressed;
[*]The color of the “Equippable by” text has been changed to red when reading the tooltip;
[*]Enemy targeting priority has been rebalanced;
[*]Items are no longer accidentally discarded by dropping them between slots on inventory and shops;
[*]Preventions against the Inventory, Help and Options buttons being displayed behind the party selection screen have been taken;
[*]Solved an issue where the "Bat-Hide Pigaciae" item was turning into "Coal Shoes" after reloading the game;
[*]Some missing colliders at “Death Siege”, “House of Penance”, “On the Edge”, “Moth’s Flame”, “Into the Fire” and “Last Rites” quests have been corrected;
[*]Tiles indicating the reach of the “Night of the Hunter” skill now appear through objects;
[*]Fixed debug text when Kentish Soldier is Burned;
[*]Caliburn’s dialogue won’t show off-screen during the cutscene if the camera is zoomed in;
[*]Credits timing has been adjusted;
[*]Tablets and consumables will always apply effects on the right target;
[*]Heroes cannot use consumables during Overwatch;
[*]The weapon rack in the “Failed Vows” quest now drops the correct weapon;
[*]After continuing the game from a checkpoint, passive skills will apply the correct stats on the heroes.
[/list]
We hope to keep enriching your journey through Broken Britannia. Please continue to help us perfect this game with your suggestions and participation Thank you for playing and being part of our community!
